{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1285020-what-would-be-special-about-a-mage-city-book","id":1285020,"title":"What would be special about a mage city book?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-05T11:38:17-08:00","id":1285020,"title":"What would be special about a mage city book?","content":"I'm thinking of taking the resources from a long-running chronicle and doing Storytellers Vault supplement on the city it takes place in. The problem is Mage has one modern city sourcebook in the form of The Fallen Tower: Las Vegas. I've read through some of the Vampire: The Masquerade sourcebooks and one note is that in The Fallen Tower, relationships between chantries seems more important than relationships between individuals. Besides that, what would be special to a mage city sourcebook?<br /> <br /> Chantries, mages of note, relationships with Sorcerers, regional rotes if any, and?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15603-phillycuriosity","name":"PhillyCuriosity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15603_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-05T13:00:28-08:00","id":1285042,"title":"","content":"Well, as an addition of M20 that I think was very needed, a city book should have details on the Reality Zones of the city.<br /> <br /> The Umbra won't be as important as in a Werewolf book, but it would be useful for some mages. Regional rotes would be nice, coupled with Paradigms of note.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-05T13:14:55-08:00","id":1285048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1285020-what-would-be-special-about-a-mage-city-book?p=1285042#post1285042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">a city book should have details on the Reality Zones of the city.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh neat, thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15603-phillycuriosity","name":"PhillyCuriosity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15603_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T08:21:17-08:00","id":1285249,"title":"","content":"Something I started including was the idea of city councils, made up of representatives of the local Chantries. This is completely optional, but I've found it made the idea of a bunch of different factions having to work together feel like more of a real and present thing instead of some abstract global concept. And it makes for fun political and even legal drama. <br /> <br /> One thing to consider is the mystic history of the city. Both real world strangeness (such as the Ripper Murders in London, or the legend of the Red Dwarf in Detroit) that may or may not be Magical in nature, but also important events in the Awakened's shadow history of the city. Infamous betrayals, major battles, remembered tragedies, etc. <br /> <br /> I also like to try to find possible ideas for Bygones that may at least be in the region if not the city itself. <br /> <br /> Acolytes of note may also be useful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T20:27:11-08:00","id":1285782,"title":"","content":"Though the Umbra isn't as important in Mage as Aleph said I feel that the type of &quot;Spirit of the City&quot; is. Obviously the larger the city the more aware and potentially powerful/influencing such a spirit would/could be. Remember that the presence of a spiritually awakened city will leave its mark on many of the everyday facets of city life. Even if only for descriptive purposes.<br /> <br /> Personally when i am the ST I run almost every town or city (and many important locations) has an awakened spirit of the location. Just HOW awakened it is, is based on my needs and desires as the ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}